<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balasore</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Baleshwar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balasore, or Baleshwar, is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>, and the headquarters of Balasore district. From the 17th century the English, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, French and Danish East India Companies kept trading factories there. The nearby coast at Chandipur is a missile testing range, and the district includes the former princely state of Nilgiri.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balasore.jpg" alt="Balasore" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Apurv013 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emami_Jagannath_Temple,_Balasore,_Odisha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
